IMPORT prelude

-- Codex Insurance Limited -- hospitalization policy.
--
-- Every date/time fact about a claim is expressed as a NUMBER of months
-- elapsed since the policy's effective date. Every deadline in the source
-- text is itself stated as a month-anniversary of the effective date (the
-- 6th month, the 7th month, one year), so no rule here ever needs the time
-- elapsed BETWEEN two absolute dates -- each time fact is already relative
-- to the one date that matters. The sole exception is the claimant's age,
-- an absolute NUMBER of years.
--
-- Section 1.1 items (1) "this agreement is signed" and (2) "the applicable
-- premium for the policy period has been paid" are, per the encoding brief,
-- always assumed true and are not modelled as fields or rules below.

DECLARE HospitalizationClaim HAS
    `age at hospitalization`             IS A NUMBER
    `hospitalization time`               IS A NUMBER
    `caused by skydiving`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused by military service`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused by firefighter service`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused by police service`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `fraudulent`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `misrepresented`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `withheld information`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `wellness visit time`                IS A NUMBER
    `wellness visit confirmation time`   IS A NUMBER

§ `Policy in Effect and Conditions`

§§ `1.1 -- the policy is in effect at the time of the hospitalization`

-- Item (3) is `section 1.3 condition satisfied` below; item (4) is
-- "not canceled", i.e. NOT `policy canceled`. Items (1)-(2) are assumed.
GIVEN claim IS A HospitalizationClaim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `policy in effect` IF
        `section 1.3 condition satisfied` claim
    AND NOT (`policy canceled` claim)

§§ `1.2 -- cancelation`

GIVEN claim IS A HospitalizationClaim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `policy canceled` IF
        `fraud misrepresentation or withholding` claim
    OR  NOT (`section 1.3 condition satisfied` claim)
    OR  `policy term has expired` claim

-- "there is fraud, or any misrepresentation or material withholding of any
-- information provided by you to the Company in connection with any
-- communication or information relating to this policy"
GIVEN claim IS A HospitalizationClaim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `fraud misrepresentation or withholding` IF
        claim's `fraudulent`
    OR  claim's `misrepresented`
    OR  claim's `withheld information`

-- The one-year term comes from Section 3.6 below ("Policy Term"); automatic
-- cancelation on expiry is confirmed by the last sentence of 1.2.
GIVEN claim IS A HospitalizationClaim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `policy term has expired` IF
    claim's `hospitalization time` GREATER THAN 12

§§ `1.3 -- the wellness-visit condition`

-- "No later than the 7th month anniversary of the effective date ... you
-- will supply us with written confirmation ... of a wellness visit ...
-- occurring no later than the 6th month anniversary of the effective date."
-- Two separate deadlines: the visit itself (<= 6 months) and the written
-- confirmation of it (<= 7 months).
GIVEN claim IS A HospitalizationClaim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 1.3 condition satisfied` IF
        claim's `wellness visit time` AT MOST 6
    AND claim's `wellness visit confirmation time` AT MOST 7

§ `General Exclusions`

§§ `2.1 -- events for which no benefit is paid`

-- Each ground below tests what CAUSED the hospitalization, not the
-- claimant's occupation or status in the abstract: e.g. a serving police
-- officer hospitalized for a reason unconnected to police service is not
-- caught by ground (4), because the text excludes sickness/injury "arising
-- directly or indirectly out of" the listed activity, not the claimant's
-- job title. Each ground is therefore its own fact about causation.
GIVEN claim IS A HospitalizationClaim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `hospitalization excluded` IF
        claim's `caused by skydiving`
    OR  claim's `caused by military service`
    OR  claim's `caused by firefighter service`
    OR  claim's `caused by police service`
    OR  claim's `age at hospitalization` AT LEAST 80

-- Section 3.1.1 ("insures You twenty-four (24) hours a day anywhere in the
-- world") means location is never a further condition on coverage, so no
-- field or rule for it is needed above.

-- Top-level decision: does the policy cover this hospitalization claim?
GIVEN claim IS A HospitalizationClaim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `covered` IF
        `policy in effect` claim
    AND NOT (`hospitalization excluded` claim)
